1. Introduction
 * Purpose: The purpose of this project (project.py) is to automate Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), data cleaning, missing-value imputation, feature engineering, and memory optimization on the raw Titanic dataset (Titanic-Dataset.csv).
 * Scope: The program processes 891 raw passenger records, removes missing and redundant fields, optimizes column data types, and generates a 100% clean output dataset (Titanic-Cleaned.csv).
2. System & Software Requirements
 * Programming Language: Python 3.10+
 * Libraries Used: pandas
 * Tools & Platforms: Visual Studio Code, Git, GitHub
 * Operating System: Windows 10 / 11
3. Functional Requirements
   * Remove duplicate rows via drop_duplicates().
   * Drop non-predictive ID columns (PassengerId, Name, Ticket) and the sparsely populated Cabin column (77.1% empty).
   * Impute 177 missing Age values using grouped median by Pclass and Sex.
   * Impute 2 missing Embarked values using statistical mode ('S').
 * Feature Engineering (FR-3): Create FamilySize (SibSp + Parch + 1) and IsAlone (1 if FamilySize == 1, else 0).
 * Memory Optimization (FR-4): Downcast integer columns to int8, float columns to float32, and low-cardinality text columns (Sex, Embarked) to category, reducing memory usage by over 95%.
 * Data Export (FR-5): Export the final cleaned dataset (891 rows × 10 columns, 0 null cells) to Titanic-Cleaned.csv with index=False.
4. Input & Output Summary
 * Input File: Titanic-Dataset.csv (891 rows × 12 columns, 866 missing cells, ~315 KB)
 * Output File: Titanic-Cleaned.csv (891 rows × 10 columns, 0 missing cells, ~14.5 KB)
